{
 "$comment": [
  "The ONE definition of every parity case: stored goldens and differential-only argv rows alike.",
  "AUTHORED. Nothing regenerates this file. It replaced capture.py's CASES table, cases.mjs's",
  "EXTRA_CASES and cases.mjs's GOLDEN_CAPABILITY, which were three parallel descriptions of one",
  "matrix; a case added to one of them was invisible to the others.",
  "captureAnchor is present exactly when storedGolden is true, and is the wall clock the golden",
  "was captured under - relative-date cases are only reproducible against a pinned 'today'. It is",
  "per-case on purpose: a single top-level anchor would be a second place for the value to live,",
  "and the per-case field is the one capture.py and the parity harness actually read.",
  "comparisonPolicy names a handler in tests-ts/harness/policies.mjs; waiver must equal that",
  "policy's declared waiverId, so a comparison can never grant itself an unauthorised licence.",
  "'waiver': null is written explicitly, never omitted - an absent field would make 'authorised",
  "by nothing' and 'needs no authorisation' the same state on disk."
 ],
